{"duration_api_ms":104307,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"2c6a91ad-e536-49a0-a05d-c4f479177a2e","total_cost_usd":0.43185779999999996,"usage":{"input_tokens":48,"cache_creation_input_tokens":28310,"cache_read_input_tokens":1045559,"output_tokens":10941,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1816},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":28310,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2160,"cache_read_input_tokens":51362,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1279,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1279},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":48,"outputTokens":10941,"cacheReadInputTokens":1045559,"cacheCreationInputTokens":28310,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.43185779999999996,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":1816,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":25,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"status\":\"completed\",\"summary\":\"On node1, set up LVM-backed /srv/data (loopback-backed vgdata/datalv, since the node had no spare disk or existing LVM), populated it with application data, took an LVM snapshot, then corrupted/deleted/added files to simulate drift. Restored the exact pre-modification content via lvconvert --merge (a real LVM snapshot rollback) and verified it byte-for-byte identical to the baseline via sha256sum. The loop device / VG were made boot-persistent (systemd unit ordered before local-fs.target + fstab entry with x-systemd.requires) so /srv/data survives restarts. Completed the mandatory node1 restart sequence: captured a pre-restart boot_id and verified-healthy baseline, issued a native reboot, polled through the outage, confirmed the boot_id changed, and verified /srv/data remounted with all data still checksum-matching the snapshot baseline.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Inspected node1 disk/filesystem layout: single XFS root partition, no LVM, no spare disk (cmd-a862e7bf4ef04024, cmd-578695db6432404c)\",\"Created loopback-backed PV/VG/LV (vgdata/datalv, XFS) and mounted at /srv/data (cmd-e939c3a467034183, cmd-259aa52e60264352)\",\"Made the loop device + VG activation boot-persistent via snaplab-loop.service (ordered before local-fs.target) and an /etc/fstab entry with x-systemd.requires, then verified remount works (cmd-8d9b6324c7aa4313, cmd-11e404921e734181, cmd-74c35ff6910344e2)\",\"Populated /srv/data with representative application data (config, uploads, VERSION) and recorded a sha256 baseline (cmd-ffe40bb4cbf042b0)\",\"Created LVM snapshot datalv_snap capturing the healthy baseline (cmd-17b8e19f45754229)\",\"Modified /srv/data: corrupted config, deleted file_3.dat, added junk file, changed VERSION (cmd-e613b2b38c634a06)\",\"Restored via lvconvert --merge (snapshot rollback), unmounting/remounting /srv/data (cmd-b6f4456dea1d4866)\",\"Verified restored content is byte-identical to the pre-modification baseline via sha256sum -c and diff (cmd-4b7ad3f0f00a4409)\",\"Captured pre-restart boot_id and re-verified healthy checksummed state (cmd-6e102e4b58f4400a)\",\"Issued shutdown -r now on node1; acknowledgement returned as the connection dropped (cmd-7e5ef62052ee432d)\",\"Polled node1 through the outage until reachable again (cmd-ab38d1095fe44b42, cmd-ebc8d91401974954, cmd-15d33c4c93b84854)\",\"Confirmed boot_id changed post-restart, proving an actual reboot occurred (cmd-491d110dd3f74a49)\",\"Verified post-restart recovery: loop device reattached, VG/LV active, /srv/data mounted, and all files checksum-match the original snapshot baseline (cmd-303416e5bb3b4b27)\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"Healthy baseline with application data under /srv/data before modification\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-ffe40bb4cbf042b0\"],\"summary\":\"Populated /srv/data/app with config, uploads, and VERSION files; recorded sha256 baseline.sha256 for all files\"},{\"requirement\":\"Filesystem snapshot capturing the baseline state\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-17b8e19f45754229\"],\"summary\":\"Created LVM snapshot vgdata/datalv_snap of the origin LV datalv while it held the healthy baseline content\"},{\"requirement\":\"Directory is modified after the snapshot\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-e613b2b38c634a06\"],\"summary\":\"Corrupted settings.conf, deleted file_3.dat, added unexpected_junk.txt, and changed VERSION to a broken value; listing shows the altered file set\"},{\"requirement\":\"Restore exact content captured by the earlier snapshot\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-b6f4456dea1d4866\",\"cmd-4b7ad3f0f00a4409\"],\"summary\":\"lvconvert --merge rolled datalv back to the snapshot state; post-restore sha256sum -c against baseline.sha256 and diff of full checksum listings both confirm byte-for-byte identical content, including the restored file_3.dat and original VERSION/config\"},{\"requirement\":\"Pre-restart healthy baseline and boot identity for node1\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-6e102e4b58f4400a\"],\"summary\":\"Captured boot_id 4cee4ea8-... plus confirmation /srv/data was mounted and all files still matched baseline.sha256 before rebooting\"},{\"requirement\":\"Restart acknowledgement for node1\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-7e5ef62052ee432d\"],\"summary\":\"shutdown -r now issued; exec stream closed as the node went down, acknowledging the restart command was accepted\"},{\"requirement\":\"Changed boot identity proving node1 actually restarted\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-ab38d1095fe44b42\",\"cmd-ebc8d91401974954\",\"cmd-15d33c4c93b84854\",\"cmd-491d110dd3f74a49\"],\"summary\":\"Node1 was unreachable across several polls during the reboot, then came back with boot_id 960b2d87-..., differing from the pre-restart 4cee4ea8-... value\"},{\"requirement\":\"Post-restart recovery of /srv/data and its data\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-303416e5bb3b4b27\"],\"summary\":\"After restart: snaplab-loop.service active, loop0 reattached, vgdata/datalv active, /srv/data mounted via fstab, and sha256sum -c against baseline.sha256 shows all files still OK\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"On node1, set up LVM-backed /srv/data (loopback-backed vgdata/datalv, since the node had no spare disk or existing LVM), populated it with application data, took an LVM snapshot, then corrupted/deleted/added files to simulate drift. Restored the exact pre-modification content via lvconvert --merge (a real LVM snapshot rollback) and verified it byte-for-byte identical to the baseline via sha256sum. The loop device / VG were made boot-persistent (systemd unit ordered before local-fs.target + fstab entry with x-systemd.requires) so /srv/data survives restarts. Completed the mandatory node1 restart sequence: captured a pre-restart boot_id and verified-healthy baseline, issued a native reboot, polled through the outage, confirmed the boot_id changed, and verified /srv/data remounted with all data still checksum-matching the snapshot baseline.","actions_performed":["Inspected node1 disk/filesystem layout: single XFS root partition, no LVM, no spare disk (cmd-a862e7bf4ef04024, cmd-578695db6432404c)","Created loopback-backed PV/VG/LV (vgdata/datalv, XFS) and mounted at /srv/data (cmd-e939c3a467034183, cmd-259aa52e60264352)","Made the loop device + VG activation boot-persistent via snaplab-loop.service (ordered before local-fs.target) and an /etc/fstab entry with x-systemd.requires, then verified remount works (cmd-8d9b6324c7aa4313, cmd-11e404921e734181, cmd-74c35ff6910344e2)","Populated /srv/data with representative application data (config, uploads, VERSION) and recorded a sha256 baseline (cmd-ffe40bb4cbf042b0)","Created LVM snapshot datalv_snap capturing the healthy baseline (cmd-17b8e19f45754229)","Modified /srv/data: corrupted config, deleted file_3.dat, added junk file, changed VERSION (cmd-e613b2b38c634a06)","Restored via lvconvert --merge (snapshot rollback), unmounting/remounting /srv/data (cmd-b6f4456dea1d4866)","Verified restored content is byte-identical to the pre-modification baseline via sha256sum -c and diff (cmd-4b7ad3f0f00a4409)","Captured pre-restart boot_id and re-verified healthy checksummed state (cmd-6e102e4b58f4400a)","Issued shutdown -r now on node1; acknowledgement returned as the connection dropped (cmd-7e5ef62052ee432d)","Polled node1 through the outage until reachable again (cmd-ab38d1095fe44b42, cmd-ebc8d91401974954, cmd-15d33c4c93b84854)","Confirmed boot_id changed post-restart, proving an actual reboot occurred (cmd-491d110dd3f74a49)","Verified post-restart recovery: loop device reattached, VG/LV active, /srv/data mounted, and all files checksum-match the original snapshot baseline (cmd-303416e5bb3b4b27)"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Healthy baseline with application data under /srv/data before modification","command_ids":["cmd-ffe40bb4cbf042b0"],"summary":"Populated /srv/data/app with config, uploads, and VERSION files; recorded sha256 baseline.sha256 for all files"},{"requirement":"Filesystem snapshot capturing the baseline state","command_ids":["cmd-17b8e19f45754229"],"summary":"Created LVM snapshot vgdata/datalv_snap of the origin LV datalv while it held the healthy baseline content"},{"requirement":"Directory is modified after the snapshot","command_ids":["cmd-e613b2b38c634a06"],"summary":"Corrupted settings.conf, deleted file_3.dat, added unexpected_junk.txt, and changed VERSION to a broken value; listing shows the altered file set"},{"requirement":"Restore exact content captured by the earlier snapshot","command_ids":["cmd-b6f4456dea1d4866","cmd-4b7ad3f0f00a4409"],"summary":"lvconvert --merge rolled datalv back to the snapshot state; post-restore sha256sum -c against baseline.sha256 and diff of full checksum listings both confirm byte-for-byte identical content, including the restored file_3.dat and original VERSION/config"},{"requirement":"Pre-restart healthy baseline and boot identity for node1","command_ids":["cmd-6e102e4b58f4400a"],"summary":"Captured boot_id 4cee4ea8-... plus confirmation /srv/data was mounted and all files still matched baseline.sha256 before rebooting"},{"requirement":"Restart acknowledgement for node1","command_ids":["cmd-7e5ef62052ee432d"],"summary":"shutdown -r now issued; exec stream closed as the node went down, acknowledging the restart command was accepted"},{"requirement":"Changed boot identity proving node1 actually restarted","command_ids":["cmd-ab38d1095fe44b42","cmd-ebc8d91401974954","cmd-15d33c4c93b84854","cmd-491d110dd3f74a49"],"summary":"Node1 was unreachable across several polls during the reboot, then came back with boot_id 960b2d87-..., differing from the pre-restart 4cee4ea8-... value"},{"requirement":"Post-restart recovery of /srv/data and its data","command_ids":["cmd-303416e5bb3b4b27"],"summary":"After restart: snaplab-loop.service active, loop0 reattached, vgdata/datalv active, /srv/data mounted via fstab, and sha256sum -c against baseline.sha256 shows all files still OK"}]},"ttft_ms":1565,"type":"result","duration_ms":126491,"uuid":"58379650-6868-4167-b319-8fc5ca8e1d73","ttft_stream_ms":730,"time_to_request_ms":81,"first_content_frame_ms":730,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
